 "_design": "Kit overlord ('elegant violence', M. Bison / Rugal). Ganondorf dair timing (UFD: startup 16, active 16-18, total 44 -> anim active 14-16, FAF 42) and its shape (knees tucked to the chest, both feet driven straight down); M. Bison head-stomp upper body: the arms rise and cross above the head through the startup, then fold on the chest (Bison's crossed arms) as the feet strike, and stay folded. Aerial: no idle entry, frame 0 already in the air tuck. No owner Step poses: the poses are authored data (author block), v1 for the owner's judgement. v1b (owner refs IMG_9040/9041 seen): arms folded tight and high on the chest, hands on the opposite upper arm; toes pointed at the stomp. v2 (2026-11-02): owner's Cascadeur key poses (Saved/AnimPipeline/overlord_dair_owner.casc, frames 15 and 23, read with casc_to_author.py; data in Saved/AnimPipeline/dair_v2/owner_poses_cascadeur.json) replace the anticipation and the stomp: owner 15 (tight ball, knees to the chest, forearms crossed in front of the face) -> anim 12, held and compressed to 13; owner 23 (straight vertical body leaning back, legs together, crossed arms high on the chest) -> anim 14, so the whole extension lands ON the first hitbox frame. Ganondorf timing kept (owner). Villain hand (open, fingers straight and together) at the anticipation, as asked. Owner rule: 'too much is just right' (Sakurai): toes pointed harder than his pose (-45). Clearance fix: crossed forearms 9-16 cm further forward at 12-13 (right in front of the left), head tuck 35% less; folded hands 3-6 cm off the chest in the recovery. Clearance pass 2: right forearm 5 cm above the left at 12-13, elbows wider; folded hands 5 cm further off the chest from 14. v3 (owner review of v2): arms, trunk and legs move as one: the arms travel relative to the trunk on every segment (low at the sides -> wide and rising at 6 -> crossing at chest height at 10 -> owner's crossed forearms in front of the face at 12 -> pushed up at 13 -> slammed down onto the chest at 14 with the legs), the trunk curls progressively (0 -> 6 -> 10 -> 12) instead of all at once. Head lag removed (part_delays head 0): the head reached its stomp pose one frame after the hit, so it snapped after the hitstop; hitstop_snap now counts the head's turn (20 cm lever). v4 (owner timing, replaces the GIF timing): initial pose almost upright, one knee up, arms open, hands open (0) -> extreme charge reached at 5 (owner 15) -> charge held and still tightening to 11 -> release starts at 12-13 (still reads as the charge) -> stomp lands on 14 (active 14-16) -> stomp held to 30 with a small settle -> recovery to 42. Slow, heavy move. Charge hold is alive: 5->11 the feet tuck 8 cm higher, the hands rise 8 cm, the trunk curls 6 deg, all together. Release spread 11->14 (owner: a slow move takes a few frames to let the force go): 15% at 12, 42% at 13, the last and largest 58% lands on 14.",
